t read one of them (a Read or Both row, or the restriction list of Data.Records.Get) gets that section as null. A resource, employee or manager named in the Bifrost user setup is not found through those fields and is not affected. In the same way warehouseLocations is null when the caller may not read Warehouse Employee User ID, and pendingApprovals is null when the caller may not read Approval Entry Approver ID or Status. The Bifrost user setup of the user overrides the standard links: its Resource No., Salesperson Code, Employee No., G/L Account No., Customer No., Vendor No. and Contact No. win over User Setup and the time sheet owner. Sections are null, not left out, when they cannot be filled. The answer does not include socialSecurityNo. Dependent apps can add their own top-level properties to the answer. A dependent app adds telegramChatId, a string: the Telegram chat id on the user's Bifrost user setup, or an empty string when none is set. Playbooks read it as @_who.telegramChatId. The answer has no telegramChatId when that app is not installed."
